{"availability":"available","full":"inertiajs/inertia","name":"inertia","description":"Inertia.js lets you quickly build modern single-page React, Vue and Svelte apps using classic server-side routing and controllers.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":8125,"forks":561,"created":"2019-03-06T18:43:43Z","updated":"2026-10-09T20:22:54Z","license":"MIT","branch":"3.x","homepage":"https://inertiajs.com","topics":[],"demo":"https://demo-v3.inertiajs.com/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:17.717Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:17.717Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:17.717Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T23:11:17.717Z","stars":8125,"forks":561}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Inertia.js lets builders ship modern single-page applications in React, Vue, or Svelte without building an API. Your backend keeps doing what it already does well: routing, controllers, models, authorization, validation. Instead of returning a template, it returns a page component with its data. Inertia connects the two halves, so a click never triggers a full page reload.","It all stays in one application: one codebase, one router, one source of truth, and the single-page experience your users expect. Fewer moving parts means fewer decisions between an idea and a production application, whether a human or an agent is writing the code.","Everything a real product needs, designed to work together:"],"features":["Page visits, forms, file uploads with progress, and server-side validation","Optimistic updates that render before the server responds and roll back if it fails","Partial reloads, deferred props, prefetching, polling, and infinite scroll","Server-side rendering, code splitting, and view transitions","History encryption for pages that hold sensitive data"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/inertiajs/inertia/blob/3.x/README.md","fingerprint":"8a0e338299389095b162fa7d0956cde98b8493eaeaf75d9a8c6bd7fa9f3f662e","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:17.818Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:17.818Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Inertia.js lets builders ship modern single-page applications in React, Vue, or Svelte without building an API. Your backend keeps doing what it already does well: routing, controllers, models, authorization, validation. Instead of returning a template, it returns a page component with its data. Inertia connects the two halves, so a click never triggers a full page reload.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/inertiajs/inertia/blob/3.x/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"A new application begins with login, registration, password resets, email verification, two-factor authentication, and profile settings already working.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/inertiajs/inertia/blob/3.x/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"8a0e338299389095b162fa7d0956cde98b8493eaeaf75d9a8c6bd7fa9f3f662e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/inertiajs/inertia/blob/3.x/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:17.818Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T20:22:54Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/inertiajs/inertia/blob/3.x/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:17.818Z","hash":"8a0e338299389095b162fa7d0956cde98b8493eaeaf75d9a8c6bd7fa9f3f662e","originalBytes":4271,"storedBytes":4271,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["inertia","application","inertia.js","laravel","code","one","under","vue","adapters","already","backend","page","react","security","server","svelte","between","build","built","cloud","community","conduct","contributing","data","fewer","forms","full","how","idea","license","means","month","pages","please","prefetching","production","read","repository.","review","server-side","single-page","source","starter","while","works","abide","about","adapter","adapters.","add","adonisjs","agent","anywhere","api.","app","applications","asset","authenticati